# A zero at @HEAD whose side query is cut gets the default-branch note, not the
# pinned one.
args: search 'repo:sego-fake/hz@HEAD foo'
exit: 0
--- stdout
0 matches  0.2 s
query  repo:sego-fake/hz@HEAD foo
--- stderr
sego: note: the search can't tell which files it skipped; files over 1 MiB and files with too many distinct trigrams are never searched
